IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 11 to 13: anticipatory exercise of powers, reference to Acts, citation of Acts.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.

§ `s 11: anticipatory exercise of powers`

DECLARE `Kind of power exercised before its provision commences` IS ONE OF
    `a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character`
    `a power to give or serve a notice or other document`
    `a power to appoint a person to a specified office`
    `a power to establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not`
    `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the Act`

-- src:197 | (1) Where a provision of an Act does not commence on the passing of the Act and that provision would, if it had commenced, confer power to –
-- src:199 | (a) make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character;
-- src:201 | (b) give or serve a notice or other document;
-- src:203 | (c) appoint a person to a specified office;
-- src:205 | (d) establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not; or
-- src:207 | (e) do any other thing for the purposes of the Act –
-- src:209 | then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may, notwithstanding that that provision has not commenced, but subject to subsections (3) and (4), be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act to the extent that it is necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Act, or specified provisions of the Act, into operation, or giving full effect to the Act, or specified provisions of the Act, when or after that provision commences.
@ref s 11(1) (src:197-209)
GIVEN `the provision does not commence on the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or specified provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them when or after the provision commences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` `the provision does not commence on the passing of the Act` `the contrary intention appears` `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act` `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or specified provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them when or after the provision commences` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the provision does not commence on the passing of the Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act` AND `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or specified provisions into operation, or giving full effect to them when or after the provision commences` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:211 | (2) Where –
-- src:213 | (a) a provision of an Act does not commence on the passing of the Act and the provision would, if it had commenced, amend another Act; and
-- src:215 | (b) a provision of that other Act would, if the first-mentioned provision had commenced, confer power to –
-- src:217 | (i) make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character;
-- src:219 | (ii) give or serve a notice or other document;
-- src:221 | (iii) appoint a person to a specified office;
-- src:223 | (iv) establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not; or
-- src:225 | (v) do any other thing for the purposes of that other Act –
-- src:227 | then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may, notwithstanding that the first-mentioned provision has not commenced, but subject to subsections (3) and (4), be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act in which the first-mentioned provision is contained to the extent that it is necessary or expedient for the purpose of giving full effect to that other Act, or specified provisions of that other Act, when or after the first-mentioned provision commences.
@ref s 11(2) (src:211-227)
GIVEN `the first-mentioned provision does not commence on the passing of the Act and would, if it had commenced, amend another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the other Act would, if the first-mentioned provision had commenced, confer the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act containing the first-mentioned provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is necessary or expedient for giving full effect to the other Act or specified provisions of it when or after the first-mentioned provision commences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` `the first-mentioned provision does not commence on the passing of the Act and would, if it had commenced, amend another Act` `a provision of the other Act would, if the first-mentioned provision had commenced, confer the power` `the contrary intention appears` `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act containing the first-mentioned provision` `the exercise is necessary or expedient for giving full effect to the other Act or specified provisions of it when or after the first-mentioned provision commences` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the first-mentioned provision does not commence on the passing of the Act and would, if it had commenced, amend another Act` AND `a provision of the other Act would, if the first-mentioned provision had commenced, confer the power`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the power is exercised after the passing of the Act containing the first-mentioned provision` AND `the exercise is necessary or expedient for giving full effect to the other Act or specified provisions of it when or after the first-mentioned provision commences` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of two days` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- src:229 | (3) Where a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character, or to give or serve a notice or other document, is exercised as provided in subsection (1) or in subsection (2), that instrument, notice, or document shall take effect –
-- src:231 | (a) on the day on which the provision referred to in subsection (1) or, as the case may be, the provision first-mentioned in subsection (2) commences; or
-- src:233 | (b) on the day on which it would have taken effect, if at the time when the instrument was made or the notice or document was served, the provision so mentioned or first-mentioned had commenced –
-- src:235 | whichever is the later.
@ref s 11(3) (src:229-235)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power exercised before its provision commences`
      `the day the provision referred to in subsection (1) or the first-mentioned provision in subsection (2) commences` IS A DATE
      `the day the instrument, notice or document would have taken effect if the provision had commenced when it was made or served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 11(3): the day an instrument, notice or document made or served under an anticipatory power takes effect` kind `the day the provision referred to in subsection (1) or the first-mentioned provision in subsection (2) commences` `the day the instrument, notice or document would have taken effect if the provision had commenced when it was made or served` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` OR kind EQUALS `a power to give or serve a notice or other document`
    THEN JUST (`the later of two days` `the day the provision referred to in subsection (1) or the first-mentioned provision in subsection (2) commences` `the day the instrument, notice or document would have taken effect if the provision had commenced when it was made or served`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:237 | (4) Where a power to appoint a person to a specified office, or to establish a specified body of persons, is exercised as provided in subsection (1) or subsection (2), the person so appointed may act in that office, or, as the case may be, the body so established may meet and perform and exercise its functions, duties, and powers, but only for a purpose referred to in subsection (1) or subsection (2) (whichever of those subsections is applicable).
@ref s 11(4) (src:237)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of power exercised before its provision commences`
      `the appointment or establishment was made under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts, or the body meets and performs its functions, for a purpose referred to in subsection (1) or (2) (whichever applies)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` kind `the appointment or establishment was made under subsection (1) or (2)` `the person acts, or the body meets and performs its functions, for a purpose referred to in subsection (1) or (2) (whichever applies)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (kind EQUALS `a power to appoint a person to a specified office` OR kind EQUALS `a power to establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the appointment or establishment was made under subsection (1) or (2)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the person acts, or the body meets and performs its functions, for a purpose referred to in subsection (1) or (2) (whichever applies)` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(1): the power may be exercised although the provision conferring it has not commenced` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(2): the power under the other Act may be exercised although the amending provision has not commenced` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the day an instrument, notice or document made or served under an anticipatory power takes effect` `a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the day an instrument, notice or document made or served under an anticipatory power takes effect` `a power to give or serve a notice or other document` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the day an instrument, notice or document made or served under an anticipatory power takes effect` `a power to make an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT `s 11(3): the day an instrument, notice or document made or served under an anticipatory power takes effect` `a power to appoint a person to a specified office` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` `a power to appoint a person to a specified office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` `a power to establish a specified body of persons, whether incorporated or not` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` `a power to appoint a person to a specified office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` `a power to appoint a person to a specified office` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(4): the person appointed may act in the office, or the body established may meet and perform its functions` `a power to give or serve a notice or other document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 12: reference to Acts`

DECLARE `Parliament that passed an Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Parliament of Tasmania`
    `the Parliament of the United Kingdom or the Parliament of England`
    `the Parliament of the Commonwealth`

-- src:241 | (1) An Act passed by the Parliament of Tasmania may, in any Act, instrument, or document, be referred to by the word "Act" alone.
-- src:243 | (2) An Act passed by the Parliament of the United Kingdom or the Parliament of England, as the case may be, may, in any Act, instrument, or document, be referred to by the term "Imperial Act".
-- src:245 | (3) An Act passed by the Parliament of the Commonwealth may, in any Act, instrument, or document, be referred to by the term "Commonwealth Act" or "Act of the Commonwealth".
@ref s 12(1), (2) and (3) (src:241-245)
GIVEN parliament IS A `Parliament that passed an Act`
      term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` parliament term MEANS
    BRANCH IF parliament EQUALS `the Parliament of Tasmania` AND term EQUALS "Act" THEN JUST TRUE
           IF parliament EQUALS `the Parliament of the United Kingdom or the Parliament of England` AND term EQUALS "Imperial Act" THEN JUST TRUE
           IF parliament EQUALS `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` AND (term EQUALS "Commonwealth Act" OR term EQUALS "Act of the Commonwealth") THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of Tasmania` "Act" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of the United Kingdom or the Parliament of England` "Imperial Act" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` "Commonwealth Act" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` "Act of the Commonwealth" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of Tasmania` "Imperial Act" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12: an Act passed by the Parliament may be referred to by the term` `the Parliament of the Commonwealth` "Imperial Act" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 13: citation of Acts`

DECLARE `Way of citing an Act` IS ONE OF
    `by its short title`
    `by its short title, together with a reference to that State or Territory`
    `by reference to the regnal year in which it is passed`
    `by reference to the calendar year in which it is passed`
    `by its number`
    `by reference to the regnal year in which it was passed and its chapter, together with a reference to the United Kingdom`
    `by reference to the calendar year in which it was passed and its number, together with a reference to the Commonwealth`
    `in such other manner as is sufficient in an Act or Ordinance of that State or Territory, together with a reference to that State or Territory`

-- src:249 | (1) In any Act, instrument, or document –
-- src:251 | (a) an Act may be cited –
-- src:253 | (i) by its short title or by reference to the regnal year or calendar year in which it is passed; and
-- src:255 | (ii) by its number;
-- src:257 | (b) any Imperial Act may be cited by its short title, if any, or by reference to the regnal year in which it was passed and its chapter, together with a reference to the United Kingdom; and
-- src:259 | (c) any Commonwealth Act may be cited by its short title, if any, or by reference to the calendar year in which it was passed and its number, together with a reference to the Commonwealth; and
-- src:261 | (d) any Act or Ordinance of another State or Territory may be cited –
-- src:263 | (i) by its short title, if any; or
-- src:265 | (ii) in such other manner as is sufficient in an Act or Ordinance of that State or Territory –
-- src:267 | together with a reference to that State or Territory.
@ref s 13(1) (src:249-267)
GIVEN `the Act` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the Act has a short title` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `Way of citing an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1): an Act of the kind may be cited in the way` `the Act` `the Act has a short title` way MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the Act` EQUALS `an Act` AND (way EQUALS `by its short title` OR way EQUALS `by reference to the regnal year in which it is passed` OR way EQUALS `by reference to the calendar year in which it is passed` OR way EQUALS `by its number`) THEN
               IF way EQUALS `by its short title` AND NOT (`the Act has a short title`) THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE
           IF `the Act` EQUALS `an Imperial Act` AND (way EQUALS `by its short title` OR way EQUALS `by reference to the regnal year in which it was passed and its chapter, together with a reference to the United Kingdom`) THEN
               IF way EQUALS `by its short title` AND NOT (`the Act has a short title`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "if any"
           IF `the Act` EQUALS `a Commonwealth Act` AND (way EQUALS `by its short title` OR way EQUALS `by reference to the calendar year in which it was passed and its number, together with a reference to the Commonwealth`) THEN
               IF way EQUALS `by its short title` AND NOT (`the Act has a short title`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "if any"
           IF `the Act` EQUALS `an Act or Ordinance of another State or Territory` AND (way EQUALS `by its short title, together with a reference to that State or Territory` OR way EQUALS `in such other manner as is sufficient in an Act or Ordinance of that State or Territory, together with a reference to that State or Territory`) THEN
               IF way EQUALS `by its short title, together with a reference to that State or Territory` AND NOT (`the Act has a short title`) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "if any"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:269 | (2) Any enactment may be cited by reference to the Part, section, subsection, or other division of the Act, Imperial Act, Commonwealth Act or Act or Ordinance of the State or Territory in which it is contained.
@ref s 13(2) (src:269)
GIVEN division IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2): an enactment may be cited by reference to the division of the Act in which it is contained` division MEANS
    IF division EQUALS "Part" OR division EQUALS "section" OR division EQUALS "subsection"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Act whose citation is checked against a copy` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of this State on the database within the meaning of the Legislation Publication Act 1996`
    `any other Act of this State`
    `any other Act or Ordinance`

-- src:271 | (3) Any reference referred to in subsections (1) and (2) is to be made –
-- src:273 | (a) in the case of an Act of this State on the database, within the meaning of the Legislation Publication Act 1996, according to a copy of the Act produced or purporting to be produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996; and
-- src:275 | (b) in the case of any other Act of this State, according to a copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer; and
-- src:277 | (c) in the case of any other Act or Ordinance, according to a copy of the Act or Ordinance printed by the official printer for the Government of the United Kingdom, the Commonwealth or the State or Territory.
@ref s 13(3) (src:271-277)
GIVEN act IS A `Act whose citation is checked against a copy`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 13(3): the copy according to which a reference in subsections (1) and (2) is made` act MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `an Act of this State on the database within the meaning of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` THEN "a copy of the Act produced or purporting to be produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996"
    WHEN `any other Act of this State` THEN "a copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer"
    WHEN `any other Act or Ordinance` THEN "a copy of the Act or Ordinance printed by the official printer for the Government of the United Kingdom, the Commonwealth or the State or Territory"

-- src:279 | (4) A description or citation in any Act of a portion of another Act shall be construed as including the words, sections, or other parts mentioned or referred to as forming the beginning and the end respectively of the portion comprised in the description or citation.
@ref s 13(4) (src:279)
GIVEN `the first section of the portion` IS A NUMBER
      `the last section of the portion` IS A NUMBER
      section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(4): a section is within the portion described or cited` `the first section of the portion` `the last section of the portion` section MEANS
    section AT LEAST `the first section of the portion` AND section AT MOST `the last section of the portion`

-- src:281 | (5) In any Act any reference to or citation of an Act shall be deemed to include a reference to or citation of all subsequent enactments passed in amendment or substitution of the Act so referred to or cited, whether those subsequent enactments are, or any of them is, passed before or after the passing of the Act in which the reference or citation occurs.
@ref s 13(5) (src:281)
GIVEN `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(5): a reference to or citation of an Act includes the later enactments passed in amendment or substitution of it, whether passed before or after the Act containing the reference` `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited` MEANS
    IF `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` AND `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:283 | (6) In any Act, a reference to or citation of an Imperial Act, a Commonwealth Act or an Act or Ordinance of another State or Territory shall be deemed to include a reference to or citation of all subsequent enactments passed in amendment or substitution of the Imperial Act, Commonwealth Act or Act or Ordinance of the State or Territory so referred to or cited, whether those subsequent enactments are, or any of them is, passed before or after the passing of the Act in which the reference occurs.
@ref s 13(6) (src:283)
GIVEN `the thing cited` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(6): a reference to or citation of an Imperial Act, Commonwealth Act or Act or Ordinance of another State or Territory includes the later enactments passed in amendment or substitution of it` `the thing cited` `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited` MEANS
    IF (`the thing cited` EQUALS `an Imperial Act` OR `the thing cited` EQUALS `a Commonwealth Act` OR `the thing cited` EQUALS `an Act or Ordinance of another State or Territory`) AND `the reference or citation occurs in an Act` AND `the later enactment is passed in amendment or substitution of the Act cited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

